WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.320
- I love that you sing
a song before, you know,

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.280
like you were saying, you
sing before you go out.

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:05.990
Why did you choose the song that you sing

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:07.200
before you go out on SNL?

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.060
And like, is there,

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:10.290
did that tradition start
with you doing that?

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:11.971
Or were you asked to do that?

00:00:11.971 --> 00:00:14.549
- No, I graduated into it.

00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:17.300
It was a thing, I think
like when I first got there

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.750
Jimmy Fallon was doing it

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.830
and he was like rocking out or something.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:21.800
Like he was a rockstar.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.810
So he was playing the
guitar and doing a song.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.820
And then Fred, when I
first started doing it

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:31.140
I started doing it with Fred
and he was playing the guitar

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.571
and I was playing like
the Congas or something.

00:00:33.571 --> 00:00:37.780
And it was me, him and Taran
Killam and we were singing

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:42.677
you know, a song from the
Clash, I want to say, but yeah,

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.880
just whoever's the
responsibility is you get to

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.540
choose whatever song you like.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.410
So Fred, you know, he's
a guitarist and, you know

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:52.390
he was in a band for real.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:55.040
So he was in like the rock
and roll kind of genre.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:57.670
And then when he left,
they were like, well,

00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:58.640
who's going to do the warmup?

00:00:58.640 --> 00:00:59.960
And I was like, yeah, I'll do it.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:02.350
And I started with like an obvious one

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:04.350
like Elton John Saturday,
you know what I mean?

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:06.550
So I sang that for
awhile and that was fun.

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:08.060
And then I moved into like, Oh,

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.470
let me start feeling my groove.

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:10.950
And I started doing
like the Doobie Brothers

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:12.410
Long Train Running and stuff like that.

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:13.520
And now we landed on

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:16.810
the Spencer Davis group,
Give Me Some Loving,

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:20.430
which is like just a solid
crowd pleaser basically.

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:21.840
And everybody seems to like it.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.100
It gets the energy going and we've been

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.740
on that for like eight years
or something like that.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.723
So it's been a minute.

